 god or pantheon. It might be an amulet depicting a symbol representing a deity, the same symbol carefully engraved or inlaid as an emblem on a shield, or a tiny box holding a fragment of a sacred relic. A cleric or a Paladin can use a holy symbol as a spellcasting focus. To use the symbol in this way, the caster must hold it in hand, wear it visibly, or bear it on a shield.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,2,2.000,0,305,1,NULL,NULL),(151,'Holy Water - flask',3,'As an action, you can splash the contents of this flask onto a creature within 5 feet of you or throw it up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. In either case, make a ranged attack against a target creature, treating the holy water as an improvised weapon. If the target is a fiend or undead, it takes 2d6 radiant damage. A cleric or paladin may create holy water by performing a special ritual. The ritual takes 1 hour to perform, uses 25 gp worth of powdered silver, and requires the caster to expend a 1st-level spell slot.',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',25,2,1.000,0,306,1,NULL,NULL),(152,'Hourglass',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',25,2,1.000,0,307,1,NULL,NULL),(153,'Hunting Trap',3,'When you use your action to set it, this trap forms a saw-toothed steel ring that snaps shut when a creature steps on a pressure plate in the center. The trap is affixed by a heavy chain to an immobile object, such as a tree or a spike driven into the ground. A creature that steps on the plate must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 1d4 piercing damage and stop moving. Thereafter until the creature breaks free of the trap, its movement is limited by the length of the chain (typically 3 feet long). A creature can use its action to make a DC 13 Strength check, freeing itself or another creature within its reach on a success. Each failed check deals 1 piercing damage to the trapped creature.',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,2,25.000,0,308,1,NULL,NULL),(154,'Ink - 1 ounce bottle',3,'',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',10,2,0.000,0,309,1,NULL,NULL),(155,'Ink pen',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',2,5,0.000,0,310,1,NULL,NULL),(156,'Jug / Pitcher',3,'1 gallon liquid',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '',_binary '\0',2,5,4.000,0,311,1,NULL,NULL),(157,'Ladder - 10-foot',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',1,4,25.000,0,312,1,NULL,NULL),(158,'Lamp',3,'A lamp casts bright light in a 15-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. Once lit, it burns for 6 hours on a flask (1 pint) of oil.',_binary '\0',_binary '',2,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,4,1.000,0,313,1,NULL,NULL),(159,'Lantern - bullseye',3,'A bullseye lantern casts bright light in a 60-foot cone and dim light for an additional 60 feet. Once lit, it burns for 6 hours on a flask (1 pint) of oil.',_binary '\0',_binary '',2,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',10,2,2.000,0,314,1,NULL,NULL),(160,'Lantern - hooded',3,'A hooded lantern casts bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. Once lit, it burns for 6 hours on a flask (1 pint) of oil. As an action, you can lower the hood, reducing the light to dim light in a 5-foot radius.',_binary '\0',_binary '',2,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,2,2.000,0,315,1,NULL,NULL),(161,'Lock',3,'A key is provided with the lock. Without the key, a creature proficient with thieves\' tools can pick this lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity check.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',10,2,1.000,0,316,1,NULL,NULL),(162,'Magnifying Glass',3,'This lens allows a closer look at small objects. It is also useful as a substitute for flint and steel when starting fires. Lighting a fire with a magnifying glass requires light as bright as sunlight to focus, tinder to ignite, and about 5 minutes for the fire to ignite. A magnifying glass grants advantage on any ability check to appraise or inspect an item that is small or highly detailed.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',100,2,0.000,0,317,1,NULL,NULL),(163,'Manacles',3,'These metal restraints can bind a Small or Medium creature. Escaping the manacles requires a successful DC 20 Dexterity check. Breaking them requires a successful DC 20 Strength check. Each set of manacles comes with one key. Without the key, a creature proficient with thieves\' tools can pick the manacles\' lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity check. Manacles have 15 hit points.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',2,2,6.000,0,318,1,NULL,NULL),(164,'Mess Kit',3,'This tin box contains a cup and simple cutlery. The box clamps together, and one side can be used as a cooking pan and the other as a plate or shallow bowl.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',2,4,1.000,0,319,1,NULL,NULL),(165,'Mirror - steel',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,2,0.500,0,320,1,NULL,NULL),(166,'Oil - flask',3,'Oil usually comes in a clay flask that holds 1 pint. As an action, you can splash the oil in this flask onto a creature within 5 feet of you or throw it up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. Make a ranged attack against a target creature or object, treating the oil as an improvised weapon. On a hit, the target is covered in oil. If the target takes any fire damage before the oil dries (after 1 minute), the target takes an additional 5 fire damage from the burning oil. You can also pour a flask of oil on the ground to cover a 5-foot-square area, provided that the surface is level. If lit, the oil burns for 2 rounds and deals 5 fire damage to any creature that enters the area. A creature can take this damage only once per turn.',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',1,4,1.000,0,321,1,NULL,NULL),(167,'Paper - 1 sheet',3,'',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',2,4,0.000,0,322,1,NULL,NULL),(168,'Parchment - 1 sheet',3,'',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',1,4,0.000,0,333,1,NULL,NULL),(169,'Perfume - vial',3,'',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,2,0.000,0,334,1,NULL,NULL),(170,'Miner\'s Pick',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '',2,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',2,2,10.000,0,335,1,NULL,NULL),(171,'Piton',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,5,0.250,0,336,1,NULL,NULL),(172,'Poison - basic, vial',3,'You can use the poison in this vial to coat one slashing or piercing weapon or up to three pieces of ammunition. Applying the poison takes an action. A creature hit by the poisoned weapon or ammunition must make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or take 1d4 poison damage. Once applied, the poison retains potency for 1 minute before drying.',_binary '',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',100,2,0.000,0,337,1,NULL,NULL),(173,'Pole - 10-foot',3,'',_binary '\0',_binary '',2,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',5,5,7.000,0,338,1,NULL,NULL),(174,'Pot - iron',3,'1 gallon liquid',_binary '\0',_binary '',2,_binary '',_binary '\0',2,2,10.000,0,339,1,NULL,NULL),(175,'Pouch',3,'A cloth or leather pouch can hold up to 20 sling bullets or 50 blowgun needles, among other things. A compartmentalized pouch for holding spell components is called a component pouch. 0.2 cubic feet/6 pounds of gear',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '',_binary '\0',5,4,1.000,0,340,1,NULL,NULL),(176,'Quiver',3,'A quiver can hold up to 20 arrows.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '',_binary '\0',1,2,1.000,0,341,1,NULL,NULL),(177,'Ram - portable',3,'You can use a portable ram to break down doors. When doing so, you gain a +4 bonus on the Strength check. One other character can help you use the ram, giving you advantage on this check.',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0',4,2,35.000,0,342,1,NULL,NULL),(178,'Rations - 1 day',3,'Rations consist of dry foods suitable for extended travel, including jerky, dried fruit, hardtack, and nuts.',_bina