	(@DragonTurtleAmphibiousId, 'The dragon turtle can breathe air and water.'),
	(@DriderFeyAncestryId, 'The drider has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can''t put the drider to sleep.'),
	(@DriderSpiderClimbId, 'The drider can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@DriderSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the drider has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@DriderWebWalkerId, 'The drider ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.'),
	(@DryadMagicResistanceId, 'The dryad has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@DryadSpeakWithBeastsAndPlantsId, 'The dryad can communicate with beasts and plants as if they shared a language.'),
	(@DryadTreeStrideId, 'Once on her turn, the dryad can use 10 feet of her movement to step magically into one living tree within her reach and emerge from a second living tree within 60 feet of the first tree, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second tree. Both trees must be Large or bigger.'),
	(@DuergarDuergarResilienceId, 'The duergar has advantage on saving throws against poison, spells, and illusions, as well as to resist being charmed or paralyzed.'),
	(@DuergarSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the duergar has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@AirElementalAirFormId, 'The elemental can enter a hostile creature''s space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.'),
	(@EarthElementalEarthGlideId, 'The elemental can burrow through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While doing so, the elemental doesn''t disturb the material it moves through.'),
	(@EarthElementalSiegeMonsterId, 'The elemental deals double damage to objects and structures.'),
	(@FireElementalFireFormId, 'The elemental can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing. A creature that touches the elemental or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 5 (1d10) fire damage. In addition, the elemental can enter a hostile creature''s space and stop there. The first time it enters a creature''s space on a turn, that creature takes 5 (1d10) fire damage and catches fire; until someone takes an action to douse the fire, the creature takes 5 (1d10) fire damage at the start of each of its turns.'),
	(@FireElementalIlluminationId, 'The elemental sheds bright light in a 30- foot radius and dim light in an additional 30 feet.'),
	(@FireElementalWaterSusceptibilityId, 'For every 5 feet the elemental moves in water, or for every gallon of water splashed on it, it takes 1 cold damage.'),
	(@WaterElementalWaterFormId, 'The elemental can enter a hostile creature''s space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.'),
	(@WaterElementalFreezeId, 'If the elemental takes cold damage, it partially freezes; its speed is reduced by 20 feet until the end of its next turn.'),
	(@DrowFeyAncestryId, 'The drow has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can''t put the drow to sleep.'),
	(@DrowSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the drow has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@EttercapSpiderClimbId, 'The ettercap can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@EttercapWebSenseId, 'While in contact with a web, the ettercap knows the exact location of any other creature in contact with the same web.'),
	(@EttercapWebWalkerId, 'The ettercap ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.'),
	(@EttinTwoHeadsId, 'The ettin has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, and knocked unconscious.'),
	(@EttinWakefulId, 'When one of the ettin''s heads is asleep, its other head is awake.'),
	(@ShriekerFalseAppearanceId, 'While the shrieker remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary fungus.'),
	(@VioletFungusFalseAppearanceId, 'While the violet fungus remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary fungus.'),
	(@GargoyleFalseAppearanceId, 'While the gargoyle remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an inanimate statue.'),
	(@DjinniElementalDemiseId, 'If the djinni dies, its body disintegrates into a warm breeze, leaving behind only equipment the djinni was wearing or carrying.'),
	(@EfreetiElementalDemiseId, 'If the efreeti dies, its body disintegrates in a flash of fire and puff of smoke, leaving behind only equipment the efreeti was wearing or carrying.'),
	(@GhostEtherealSightId, 'The ghost can see 60 feet into the Ethereal Plane when it is on the Material Plane, and vice versa.'),
	(@GhostIncrporealMovementId, 'The ghost can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.'),
	(@GhastStenchId, 'Any creature that starts its turn within 5 feet of the ghast must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of its next turn. On a successful saving throw, the creature is immune to the ghast''s Stench for 24 hours'),
	(@GhastTurningDefianceId, 'The ghast and any ghouls within 30 feet of it have advantage on saving throws against effects that turn undead.'),
	(@CloudGiantKeenSmellId, 'The giant has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.'),
	(@StoneGiantStoneCamouflageId, 'The giant has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.'),
	(@StormGiantAmphibiousId, 'The giant can breathe air and water.'),
	(@GibberingMoutherAberrantGroundId, 'The ground in a 10-foot radius around the mouther is doughlike difficult terrain. Each creature that starts its turn in that area must succeed on a DC 10 Strength saving throw or have its speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn.'),
	(@GibberingMoutherGibberingId, 'The mouther babbles incoherently while it can see any creature and isn''t incapacitated. Each creature that starts its turn within 20 feet of the mouther and can hear the gibbering must succeed on a DC 10 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, the creature can''t take reactions until the start of its next turn and rolls a d8 to determine what it does during its turn. On a 1 to 4, the creature does nothing. On a 5 or 6, the creature takes no action or bonus action and uses all its movement to move in a randomly determined direction. On a 7 or 8, the creature makes a melee attack against a randomly determined creature within its reach or does nothing if it can''t make such an attack.'),
	(@GnollRampageId, 'When the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.'),
	(@DeepGnomeSvirfneblinStoneCamouflageId, 'The gnome has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.'),
	(@DeepGnomeSvirfneblinGnomeCunningId, 'The gnome has advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws against magic.'),
	(@GoblinNimbleEscapeId, 'The goblin can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.'),
	(@ClayGolemAcidAbsorptionId, 'Whenever the golem is subjected to acid damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the acid damage dealt.'),
	(@ClayGolemBerserkId, 'Whenever the golem starts its turn with 60 hit points or fewer, roll a d6. On a 6, the golem goes berserk. On each of its turns while berserk, the golem attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, the golem attacks an object, with preference for an object smaller than itself. Once the golem goes berserk, it continues to do so until it is destroyed or regains all its hit points'),
	(@ClayGolemImmutableFormId, 'The golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.'),
	(@ClayGolemMagicResistanceId, 'The golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@ClayGolemMagicWeaponsId, 'The golem''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@FleshGolemBerserkId, 'Whenever the golem starts its turn with 40 hit points or fewer, roll a d6. On a 6, the golem goes berserk. On each of its turns while berserk, the golem attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, the golem attacks an object, with preference for an object smaller than itself. Once the golem goes berserk, it continues to do so until it is destroyed or regains all its hit points.\n\nThe golem''s creator, if within 60 feet of the berserk golem, can try to calm it by speaking firmly and persuasively. The golem must be able to hear its creator, who must take an action to make a DC 15 Charisma (Persuasion) check. If the check succeeds, the golem ceases being berserk. If it takes damage while still at 40 hit points or fewer, the golem might go berserk again'),
	(@FleshGolemAdversionOfFireId, 'If the golem takes fire damage, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.'),
	(@FleshGolemImmutableFormId, 'The golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.'),
	(@FleshGolemLightningAbsorptionId, 'Whenever the golem is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.'),
	(@FleshGolemMagicResistanceId, 'The golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@FleshGolemMagicWeaponsId, 'The golem''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@IronGolemFireAbsorptionId, 'Whenever the golem is subjected to fire damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the fire damage dealt.'),
	(@IronGolemImmutableFormId, 'The golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.'),
	(@IronGolemMagicResistanceId, 'The golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@IronGolemMagicWeaponsId, 'The golem''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@StoneGolemImmutableFormId, 'The golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.'),
	(@StoneGolemMagicResistanceId, 'The golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@StoneGolemMagicWeaponsId, 'The golem''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@GorgonTramplingChargeId, 'If the gorgon moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a DC 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the gorgon can make one attack with its hooves against it as a bonus action.'),
	(@GrickStoneCamouflageId, 'The grick has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.'),
	(@GriffonKeenSightId, 'The griffon has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@GrimlockBlindSensesId, 'The grimlock can''t use its blindsight while deafened and unable to smell.'),
	(@GrimlockKeenHearingAndSmellId, 'The grimlock has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.'),
	(@GrimlockStoneCamouflageId, 'The grimlock has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.'),
	(@GreenHagAmphibiousId, 'The hag can breathe air and water.'),
	(@GreenHagMimicryId, 'The hag can mimic animal sounds and humanoid voices. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful DC 14 Wisdom (Insight) check.'),
	(@NightHagMagicResistanceId, 'The hag has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@SeeHagAmphibiousId, 'The hag can breathe air and water.'),
	(@SeeHagHorrificAppearanceId, 'Any humanoid that starts its turn within 30 feet of the hag and can see the hag''s true form must make a DC 11 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, with disadvantage if the hag is within line of sight, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature''s saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the hag''s Horrific Appearance for the next 24 hours.\n\nUnless the target is surprised or the revelation of the hag''s true form is sudden, the target can avert its eyes and avoid making the initial saving throw. Until the start of its next turn, a creature that averts its eyes has disadvantage on attack rolls against the hag.'),
	(@HellHoundKeenHearingAndSmellId, 'The hound has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.'),
	(@HellHoundPackTacticsId, 'The hound has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the hound''s allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn''t incapacitated.'),
	(@HippogriffKeenSightId, 'The hippogriff has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@HobgoblinMartialAdvantaceId, 'Once per turn, the hobgoblin can deal an extra 7 (2d6) damage to a creature it hits with a weapon attack if that creature is within 5 feet of an ally of the hobgoblin that isn''t incapacitated.'),
	(@HomunculusTelepathicBondId, 'While the homunculus is on the same plane of existence as its master, it can magically convey what it senses to its master, and the two can communicate telepathically.'),
	(@HydraHoldBreathId, 'The hydra can hold its breath for 1 hour.'),
	(@HydraMultipleHeadsId, 'The hydra has five heads. While it has more than one head, the hydra has advantage on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, and knocked unconscious.\n\nWhenever the hydra takes 25 or more damage in a single turn, one of its heads dies. If all its heads die, the hydra dies.\n\nAt the end of its turn, it grows two heads for each of its heads that died since its last turn, unless it has taken fire damage since its last turn. The hydra regains 10 hit points for each head regrown in this way.'),
	(@HydraReactiveHeadsId, 'For each head the hydra has beyond one, it gets an extra reaction that can be used only for opportunity attacks.'),
	(@HydraWakefulId, 'While the hydra sleeps, at least one of its heads is awake.'),
	(@InvisibleStalkerInvisibilityId, 'The stalker is invisible'),
	(@InvisibleStalkerFaultlessTrackerId, 'The stalker is given a quarry by its summoner. The stalker knows the direction and distance to its quarry as long as the two of them are on the same plane of existence. The stalker also knows the location of its summoner.'),
	(@KoboldSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the kobold has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@KoboldPackTacticsId, 'The kobold has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kobold''s allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn''t incapacitated.'),
	(@KrakenAmphibiousId, 'The kraken can breathe air and water.'),
	(@KrakenFreedomOfMovementId, 'The kraken ignores difficult terrain, and magical effects can''t reduce its speed or cause it to be restrained. It can spend 5 feet of movement to escape from nonmagical restraints or being grappled.'),
	(@KrakenSiegeMonsterId, 'The kraken deals double damage to objects and structures.'),
	(@LichLegendaryResistanceId, 'If the lich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.'),
	(@LichRejuvenationId, 'If it has a phylactery, a destroyed lich gains a new body in 1d10 days, regaining all its hit points and becoming active again. The new body appears within 5 feet of the phylactery.'),
	(@LichTurnResistanceId, 'The lich has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns undead.'),
	(@LizardfolkHoldBreathId, 'The lizardfolk can hold its breath for 15 minutes.'),
	(@WerebearShapechangerId, 'The werebear can use its action to polymorph into a Large bear-humanoid hybrid or into a Large bear, or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics, other than its size and AC, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@WerebearKeenSmellId, 'The werebear has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.'),
	(@WereboarShapechangerId, 'The wereboar can use its action to polymorph into a boar-humanoid hybrid or into a boar, or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics, other than its AC, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@WereboarChargeBearOrHybridFormOnlyId, 'If the wereboar moves at least 15 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with its tusks on the same turn, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.'),
	(@WereboarRelentlessId, 'If the wereboar takes 14 damage or less that would reduce it to 0 hit points, it is reduced to 1 hit point instead.'),
	(@WereratShapechangerId, 'The wererat can use its action to polymorph into a rat-humanoid hybrid or into a giant rat, or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@WereratKeenSmellId, 'The wererat has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.'),
	(@WeretigerShapechangerId, 'The weretiger can use its action to polymorph into a tiger-humanoid hybrid or into a tiger, or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@WeretigerKeenHearingAndSmellId, 'The weretiger has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.'),
	(@WeretigerPounceTigerOrHybridFormOnlyId, 'If the weretiger moves at least 15 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a claw attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the weretiger can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.'),
	(@WerewolfShapechangerId, 'The werewolf can use its action to polymorph into a wolf-humanoid hybrid or into a wolf, or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics, other than its AC, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@WerewolfKeenHearingAndSmellId, 'The werewolf has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.'),
	(@MagminDeathBurstId, 'When the magmin dies, it explodes in a burst of fire and magma. Each creature within 10 feet of it must make a DC 11 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Flammable objects that aren''t being worn or carried in that area are ignited.'),
	(@MagminIgnitedIlluminationId, 'As a bonus action, the magmin can set itself ablaze or extinguish its flames. While ablaze, the magmin sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet.'),
	(@ManticoreTailSpikeRegrowthId, 'The manticore has twenty-four tail spikes. Used spikes regrow when the manticore finishes a long rest.'),
	(@MedusaPetrifyingGazeId, 'When a creature that can see the medusa''s eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of the medusa, the medusa can force it to make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw if the medusa isn''t incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is instantly petrified. Otherwise, a creature that fails the save begins to turn to stone and is restrained. The restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on a failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until the creature is freed by the greater restoration spell or other magic.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it can''t see the medusa until the start of its next turn, when it can avert its eyes again. If the creature looks at the medusa in the meantime, it must immediately make the save.\n\nIf the medusa sees itself reflected on a polished surface within 30 feet of it and in an area of bright light, the medusa is, due to its curse, affected by its own gaze.'),
	(@DustMephitDeathBurstId, 'When the mephit dies, it explodes in a burst of dust. Each creature within 5 feet of it must then succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be blinded for 1 minute. A blinded creature can repeat the saving throw on each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.'),
	(@IceMephitDeathBurstId, 'When the mephit dies, it explodes in a burst of jagged ice. Each creature within 5 feet of it must make a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw, taking 4 (1d8) slashing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.'),
	(@IceMephitFalseAppearanceId, 'While the mephit remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary shard of ice.'),
	(@MagmaMephitDeathBurstId, 'When the mephit dies, it explodes in a burst of lava. Each creature within 5 feet of it must make a DC 11 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.'),
	(@MagmaMephitFalseAppearanceId, 'While the mephit remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary mound of magma.'),
	(@SteamMephitDeathBurstId, 'When the mephit dies, it explodes in a cloud of steam. Each creature within 5 feet of the mephit must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or take 4 (1d8) fire damage.'),
	(@MerfolkAmphibiousId, 'The merfolk can breathe air and water'),
	(@MerrowAmphibiousId, 'The merrow can breathe air and water.'),
	(@MimicShapechangerId, 'The mimic can use its action to polymorph into an object or back into its true, amorphous form. Its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@MimicAdhesiveObjectFormOnlyId, 'The mimic adheres to anything that touches it. A Huge or smaller creature adhered to the mimic is also grappled by it (escape DC 13). Ability checks made to escape this grapple have disadvantage.'),
	(@MimicFalseAppearanceObjectFormOnlyId, 'While the mimic remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary object.'),
	(@MimicGrapplerId, 'The mimic has advantage on attack rolls against any creature grappled by it.'),
	(@MinotaurChargeId, 'If the minotaur moves at least 10 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away and knocked prone.'),
	(@MinotaurLabyrinthineRecallId, 'The minotaur can perfectly recall any path it has traveled.'),
	(@MinotaurRecklessId, 'At the start of its turn, the minotaur can gain advantage on all melee weapon attack rolls it makes during that turn, but attack rolls against it have advantage until the start of its next turn.'),
	(@MummyLordMagicResistanceId, 'The mummy lord has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@MummyLordRejuvenationId, 'A destroyed mummy lord gains a new body in 24 hours if its heart is intact, regaining all its hit points and becoming active again. The new body appears within 5 feet of the mummy lord''s heart.'),
	(@GuardianNagaRejuvenationId, 'If it dies, the naga returns to life in 1d6 days and regains all its hit points. Only a wish spell can prevent this trait from functioning.'),
	(@SpiritNagaRejuvenationId, 'If it dies, the naga returns to life in 1d6 days and regains all its hit points. Only a wish spell can prevent this trait from functioning.'),
	(@NightmareConferFireResistanceId, 'The nightmare can grant resistance to fire damage to anyone riding it.'),
	(@NightmareIlluminationId, 'The nightmare sheds bright light in a 10- foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet.'),
	(@OniMagicWeaponsId, 'The oni''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@OniRegenerationId, 'The oni regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point.'),
	(@BlackPuddingAmorphousId, 'The pudding can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.'),
	(@BlackPuddingCorrosiveFormId, 'A creature that touches the pudding or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 4 (1d8) acid damage. Any nonmagical weapon made of metal or wood that hits the pudding corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal or wood that hits the pudding is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\nThe pudding can eat through 2-inch-thick, nonmagical wood or metal in 1 round.'),
	(@BlackPuddingSpiderClimbId, 'The pudding can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@GelatinousCubeOozeCubeId, 'The cube takes up its entire space. Other creatures can enter the space, but a creature that does so is subjected to the cube''s Engulf and has disadvantage on the saving throw.\n\nCreatures inside the cube can be seen but have total cover.\n\nA creature within 5 feet of the cube can take an action to pull a creature or object out of the cube. Doing so requires a successful DC 12 Strength check, and the creature making the attempt takes 10 (3d6) acid damage.\n\nThe cube can hold only one Large creature or up to four Medium or smaller creatures inside it at a time.'),
	(@GelatinousCubeTransparentId, 'Even when the cube is in plain sight, it takes a successful DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check to spot a cube that has neither moved nor attacked. A creature that tries to enter the cube''s space while unaware of the cube is surprised by the cube.'),
	(@GrayOozeAmorphousId, 'The ooze can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.'),
	(@GrayOozeCorrodeMetalId, 'Any nonmagical weapon made of metal that hits the ooze corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal that hits the ooze is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\nThe ooze can eat through 2-inch-thick, nonmagical metal in 1 round.'),
	(@GrayOozeFalseAppearanceId, 'While the ooze remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an oily pool or wet rock.'),
	(@OchreJellyAmorphousId, 'The jelly can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing'),
	(@OchreJellySpiderClimbId, 'The jelly can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@OrcAggressiveId, 'As a bonus action, the orc can move up to its speed toward a hostile creature that it can see.'),
	(@OtyughLimitedTelepathyId, 'The otyugh can magically transmit simple messages and images to any creature within 120 feet of it that can understand a language. This form of telepathy doesn''t allow the receiving creature to telepathically respond.'),
	(@OwlbearKeenSightAndSmellId, 'The owlbear has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight or smell.'),
	(@PseudodragonKeenSensesId, 'The pseudodragon has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight, hearing, or smell.'),
	(@PseudodragonMagicResistanceId, 'The pseudodragon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@PseudodragonLimitedTelepathyId, 'The pseudodragon can magically communicate simple ideas, emotions, and images telepathically with any creature within 100 feet of it that can understand a language.'),
	(@PurpleWormTunnelerId, 'The worm can burrow through solid rock at half its burrow speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.'),
	(@RakshasaLimitedMagicImmunityId, 'The rakshasa can''t be affected or detected by spells of 6th level or lower unless it wishes to be. It has advantage on saving throws against all other spells and magical effects.'),
	(@RemorhazHeatedBodyId, 'A creature that touches the remorhaz or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 10 (3d6) fire damage.'),
	(@RocKeenSightId, 'The roc has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@RoperFalseAppearanceId, 'While the roper remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal cave formation, such as a stalagmite.'),
	(@RoperGraspingTendrilsId, 'The roper can have up to six tendrils at a time. Each tendril can be attacked (AC 20; 10 hit points; immunity to poison and psychic damage). Destroying a tendril deals no damage to the roper, which can extrude a replacement tendril on its next turn. A tendril can also be broken if a creature takes an action and succeeds on a DC 15 Strength check against it.'),
	(@RoperSpiderClimbId, 'The roper can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@RustMonsterIronScentId, 'The rust monster can pinpoint, by scent, the location of ferrous metal within 30 feet of it.'),
	(@RustMonsterRustMetalId, 'Any nonmagical weapon made of metal that hits the rust monster corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal that hits the rust monster is destroyed after dealing damage.'),
	(@SahuaginBloodFrenzyId, 'The sahuagin has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn''t have all its hit points.'),
	(@SahuaginLimitedAmphibiousnessId, 'The sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.'),
	(@SahuaginSharkTelepathyId, 'The sahuagin can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.'),
	(@SalamanderHeatedBodyId, 'A creature that touches the salamander or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 7 (2d6) fire damage.'),
	(@SalamanderHeatedWeaponsId, 'Any metal melee weapon the salamander wields deals an extra 3 (1d6) fire damage on a hit (included in the attack).'),
	(@SatyrMagicResistanceId, 'The satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects'),
	(@ShadowAmorphousId, 'The shadow can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.'),
	(@ShadowShadowStealthId, 'While in dim light or darkness, the shadow can take the Hide action as a bonus action.'),
	(@ShadowSunlightWeaknessId, 'While in sunlight, the shadow has disadvantage on attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws.'),
	(@ShamblingMoundLightningAbsorptionId, 'Whenever the shambling mound is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage and regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.'),
	(@ShieldGuardianBoundId, 'The shield guardian is magically bound to an amulet. As long as the guardian and its amulet are on the same plane of existence, the amulet''s wearer can telepathically call the guardian to travel to it, and the guardian knows the distance and direction to the amulet. If the guardian is within 60 feet of the amulet''s wearer, half of any damage the wearer takes (rounded up) is transferred to the guardian.'),
	(@ShieldGuardianRegenerationId, 'The shield guardian regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point'),
	(@ShieldGuardianSpellStoringId, 'A spellcaster who wears the shield guardian''s amulet can cause the guardian to store one spell of 4th level or lower. To do so, the wearer must cast the spell on the guardian. The spell has no effect but is stored within the guardian. When commanded to do so by the wearer or when a situation arises that was predefined by the spellcaster, the guardian casts the stored spell with any parameters set by the original caster, requiring no components. When the spell is cast or a new spell is stored, any previously stored spell is lost.'),
	(@MinotaurSkeletonChargeId, 'If the skeleton moves at least 10 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away and knocked prone.'),
	(@SpecterIncorporealMovementId, 'The specter can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.'),
	(@SpecterSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the specter has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@AndrosphinxInscrutableId, 'The sphinx is immune to any effect that would sense its emotions or read its thoughts, as well as any divination spell that it refuses. Wisdom (Insight) checks made to ascertain the sphinx''s intentions or sincerity have disadvantage.'),
	(@AndrosphinxMagicWeaponsId, 'The sphinx''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@GynosphinxInscrutableId, 'The sphinx is immune to any effect that would sense its emotions or read its thoughts, as well as any divination spell that it refuses. Wisdom (Insight) checks made to ascertain the sphinx''s intentions or sincerity have disadvantage.'),
	(@GynosphinxMagicWeaponsId, 'The sphinx''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@SuccubusIncubusTelepathicBondId, 'The fiend ignores the range restriction on its telepathy when communicating with a creature it has charmed. The two don''t even need to be on the same plane of existence.'),
	(@SuccubusIncubusShapechangerId, 'The fiend can use its action to polymorph into a Small or Medium humanoid, or back into its true form. Without wings, the fiend loses its flying speed. Other than its size and speed, its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn''t transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.'),
	(@TarrasqueLegendaryResistanceId, 'If the tarrasque fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.'),
	(@TarrasqueMagicResistanceId, 'The tarrasque has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@TarrasqueReflectiveCarapaceId, 'Any time the tarrasque is targeted by a magic missile spell, a line spell, or a spell that requires a ranged attack roll, roll a d6. On a 1 to 5, the tarrasque is unaffected. On a 6, the tarrasque is unaffected, and the effect is reflected back at the caster as though it originated from the tarrasque, turning the caster into the target.'),
	(@TarrasqueSiegeMonsterId, 'The tarrasque deals double damage to objects and structures.'),
	(@TreantFalseAppearanceId, 'While the treant remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal tree.'),
	(@TreantSiegeMonsterId, 'The treant deals double damage to objects and structures.'),
	(@TrollKeenSmellId, 'The troll has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.'),
	(@TrollRegenerationId, 'The troll regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn. If the troll takes acid or fire damage, this trait doesn''t function at the start of the troll''s next turn. The troll dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn''t regenerate.'),
	(@UnicornChargeId, 'If the unicorn moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a horn attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.'),
	(@UnicornMagicResistanceId, 'The unicorn has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.'),
	(@UnicornMagicWeaponsId, 'The unicorn''s weapon attacks are magical.'),
	(@VampireShapechangerId, 'If the vampire isn''t in sunlight or running water, it can use its action to polymorph into a Tiny bat or a Medium cloud of mist, or back into its true form.\n\nWhile in bat form, the vampire can''t speak, its walking speed is 5 feet, and it has a flying speed of 30 feet. Its statistics, other than its size and speed, are unchanged. Anything it is wearing transforms with it, but nothing it is carrying does. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nWhile in mist form, the vampire can''t take any actions, speak, or manipulate objects. It is weightless, has a flying speed of 20 feet, can hover, and can enter a hostile creature''s space and stop there. In addition, if air can pass through a space, the mist can do so without squeezing, and it can''t pass through water. It has advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws, and it is immune to all nonmagical damage, except the damage it takes from sunlight'),
	(@VampireLegendaryResistanceId, 'If the vampire fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.'),
	(@VampireMistyEscapeId, 'When it drops to 0 hit points outside its resting place, the vampire transforms into a cloud of mist (as in the Shapechanger trait) instead of falling unconscious, provided that it isn''t in sunlight or running water. If it can''t transform, it is destroyed.\n\nWhile it has 0 hit points in mist form, it can''t revert to its vampire form, and it must reach its resting place within 2 hours or be destroyed. Once in its resting place, it reverts to its vampire form. It is then paralyzed until it regains at least 1 hit point. After spending 1 hour in its resting place with 0 hit points, it regains 1 hit point.'),
	(@VampireRegenerationId, 'The vampire regains 20 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point and isn''t in sunlight or running water. If the vampire takes radiant damage or damage from holy water, this trait doesn''t function at the start of the vampire''s next turn.'),
	(@VampireSpiderClimbId, 'The vampire can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@VampireVampireWeaknessesId, 'The vampire has the following flaws:\n\nForbiddance. The vampire can''t enter a residence without an invitation from one of the occupants.\n\nHarmed by Running Water. The vampire takes 20 acid damage if it ends its turn in running water.\n\nStake to the Heart. If a piercing weapon made of wood is driven into the vampire''s heart while the vampire is incapacitated in its resting place, the vampire is paralyzed until the stake is removed.\n\nSunlight Hypersensitivity. The vampire takes 20 radiant damage when it starts its turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.'),
	(@VampireSpawnRegenerationId, 'The vampire regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point and isn''t in sunlight or running water. If the vampire takes radiant damage or damage from holy water, this trait doesn''t function at the start of the vampire''s next turn.'),
	(@VampireSpawnSpiderClimbId, 'The vampire can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.'),
	(@VampireSpawnVampireWeaknessesId, 'The vampire has the following flaws:\n\nForbiddance. The vampire can''t enter a residence without an invitation from one of the occupants.\n\nHarmed by Running Water. The vampire takes 20 acid damage when it ends its turn in running water.\n\nStake to the Heart. The vampire is destroyed if a piercing weapon made of wood is driven into its heart while it is incapacitated in its resting place.\n\nSunlight Hypersensitivity. The vampire takes 20 radiant damage when it starts its turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.'),
	(@WightSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the wight has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@WilloWispConsumeLifeId, 'As a bonus action, the will-o''-wisp can target one creature it can see within 5 feet of it that has 0 hit points and is still alive. The target must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw against this magic or die. If the target dies, the will-o''-wisp regains 10 (3d6) hit points.'),
	(@WilloWispEphemeralId, 'The will-o''-wisp can''t wear or carry anything.'),
	(@WilloWispIncorporealMovementId, 'The will-o''-wisp can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.'),
	(@WilloWispVariableIlluminationId, 'The will-o''-wisp sheds bright light in a 5- to 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional number of feet equal to the chosen radius. The will-o''-wisp can alter the radius as a bonus action.'),
	(@WraithIncorporealMovementId, 'The wraith can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.'),
	(@WraithSunlightSensitivityId, 'While in sunlight, the wraith has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.'),
	(@XornEarthGlideId, 'The xorn can burrow through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While doing so, the xorn doesn''t disturb the material it moves through.'),
	(@XornStoneCamouflageId, 'The xorn has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.'),
	(@XornTreasureSenseId, 'The xorn can pinpoint, by scent, the location of precious metals and stones, such as coins and gems, within 60 feet of it.'),
	(@ZombieUndeadFortitudeId, 'If damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 + the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.'),
	(@OgreZombieUndeadFortitudeId, 'If damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 + the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.'),
